---
import RenderFrame from '../media/RenderFrame.astro';
import Fn from '../primitives/Fn.astro';
---

<section class="section materials" id="materials" aria-labelledby="materials-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Materials</p>
      <h2 id="materials-title" class="display-2">Materials render as authored</h2>
    </header>

    <ul class="materials__grid">
      <li class="mat mat--wide card">
        <RenderFrame id="mat-materialx" ratio="16 / 9" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 46vw, 92vw" />
        <div class="mat__body">
          <p class="eyebrow">MaterialX 1.39</p>
          <h3 class="mat__title">Standard Surface, OpenPBR, any pbrlib graph</h3>
          <p class="mat__text">
            740 of the 746 MaterialX 1.39 node definitions run through Nova’s shading compiler, with Karma’s
            semantics.<Fn id="materialx" /> Layering is exact per MaterialX and OpenPBR, with energy compensation.
          </p>
          <p class="caption">OpenPBR 1.1 · Standard Surface · UsdPreviewSurface · glTF PBR</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="mat mat--wide card">
        <RenderFrame id="mat-kma" ratio="16 / 9" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 46vw, 92vw" />
        <div class="mat__body">
          <p class="eyebrow">Karma Material Builder</p>
          <h3 class="mat__title">Karma’s own shading nodes</h3>
          <p class="mat__text">
            35 of Karma’s 55 <span class="mono">kma_*</span> nodes: ray switches and ray imports, ramps, hex tiling,
            Voronoi, curvature, ambient occlusion, rounded edges<Fn id="kma" />
          </p>
          <p class="caption">kma_* · ray switch · hex tiling · rounded edges</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="mat card">
        <RenderFrame id="mat-principled" ratio="4 / 3" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 30vw, 92vw" />
        <div class="mat__body">
          <p class="eyebrow">Principled Shader</p>
          <h3 class="mat__title">Houdini’s Principled Shader, natively</h3>
          <p class="mat__text">
            Parameters, textures, bump and normal maps, emission, opacity and displacement follow the Principled
            Shader’s own rules: Disney sheen and clearcoat, Schlick metal, reflectivity as an effective IOR
          </p>
          <p class="caption">principledshader::2.0 · sheen · clearcoat</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="mat card">
        <RenderFrame id="mat-vex" ratio="4 / 3" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 30vw, 92vw" />
        <div class="mat__body">
          <p class="eyebrow">VEX</p>
          <h3 class="mat__title">VEX Material Builders through a CVEX bridge</h3>
          <p class="mat__text">
            The surface function is compiled once and run in batches of 256 shading points. Its BSDF stays in VEX and is
            evaluated and sampled there. On the GPU, VEX materials render as grey stand-ins.
          </p>
          <p class="caption">CVEX · 256 points per batch · CPU</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="mat card">
        <RenderFrame id="mat-displacement" ratio="4 / 3" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 30vw, 92vw" />
        <div class="mat__body">
          <p class="eyebrow">Displacement and textures</p>
          <h3 class="mat__title">Diced from the camera, UDIMs through OpenImageIO</h3>
          <p class="mat__text">
            Float and vector displacement at Karma’s dicing quality, watertight and motion-blurred. Textures with UDIMs,
            ray-cone footprints and colour spaces decided as Karma decides them.
          </p>
          <p class="caption">vector displacement · UDIM · ray cones</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .materials__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .mat {
    grid-column: span 4;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .mat--wide {
    grid-column: span 6;
  }
  /* A picture sits flush in the card; the card's corners are its corners. */
  .mat :global(.frame) {
    border-radius: 0;
    box-shadow: inset 0 -1px 0 0 var(--line);
  }
  .mat__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    align-content: start;
    padding: 24px;
  }
  .mat__title {
    font-size: var(--t-24);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .mat__text {
    font-size: var(--t-14);
    line-height: 20px;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  .mat__text .mono {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .mat__body .caption {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .mat,
    .mat--wide {
      grid-column: span 6;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .mat,
    .mat--wide {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
